  "catalogueCode": "HB-2/009-d",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Cold, dark and entirely dry of water, with a thick nitrogen atmosphere and lakes of methane in the northern lowlands fed by a haze that rains about once a decade. The water ice here is bedrock and behaves like granite. Organic solids drift down constantly and gather at the lake margins in banks a metre deep. Whether anything is eating them is precisely the question the next survey was going to ask.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    },
    {
      "value": "<p>Mrzel svet z metanskimi jezeri in debelim dušikovim ozračjem.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "sl-SI"] }]
    }
  ],
